    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >inspired by games like <i><strong>Getting Over It</strong> </i>or <i><strong>A Difficult Game About Climbing</strong></i><strong>.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>you think you know the right way to hit a cue ball? get bent. you are going hit that [expletive deleted] ball with a sideways cue and you are going to like it. now hit that 8 ball in its sly eyes...</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3477680/extras/bcc1dae500cacd05fac771502119b15f.avif?t=1739328645\" data-has-big width=800 height=800 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>its sly mother[expletive deleted] eyes. </i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >climb up and fall down.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >in scratched! you slowly but surely push your cue ball of a series of platforms using a cue. platforms that the ball can very easily roll down on, all the way to the bottom. there are no checkpoints. success in scratched! requires learning how to handle your ball and your cue to push at the exact right position at the exact right time. in other words, it's time to put the work in.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
